{"resourceIdentifier":"3822","resourceName":"Reforestation for multiple purposes as a means of sustainable development","description":"The grouped project “Reforestation program for multiple purposes as a means of sustainable development”, also known as “Plante com a Klabin” (Plant with Klabin), has as its stated goal the promotion of sustainable reforestation in Southern Brazil, specifically in the states of Paraná and Santa Catarina, aiming to achieve net removals of greenhouse gases from the atmosphere. \r\nThe land use that has historically predominated in these states is agriculture and cattle raising. The project proposes a change in the traditional land use of this region, promoting reforestation practices as a sustainable alternative, either to produce wood for multiple purposes based on rapid-growth species (for example, Pinus.spp or Eucalyptus.spp), and/or to restore areas based on native species. \r\nThrough an integrated approach, the project has established a set of incentives to make reforestation activities more attractive, with the aim to achieve important synergies between production and restoration, contributing to the strengthening of the low carbon economy and promotion of sustainable development.","location":{"latitude":-24.712803,"longitude":-51.538305},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-05-16","endExclusive":"2023-06-16","endInclusive":"2023-06-15"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3822"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Paraná, Santa Catarina"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Klabin SA"},{"type":"string","value":"São Paulo, Brazil"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Withdrawn"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2026"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"t